card.statement:
Let $V$ be a separable locally convex Hausdorff topological vector space in duality $<\cdot,\cdot>$ with $V^*$ and biorthogonal system $\{e_k,f_k\}_{k=1}^{\infty}$. Define the Jordan-Schwinger map as follows

\begin{equation}
D(A):=\sum\limits_{\alpha,\beta\in \mathbb{N}}<Ae_{\alpha},f_{\beta}> s_{\alpha} s_{\beta}^*, \quad A\in \mathcal{L}(V,V),
\end{equation}

\begin{equation}
\partial(f):= \sum\limits_{\beta\in \mathbb{N}}<f,f_{\beta}> s_{\beta}^*, f\in V,
\end{equation}

\begin{equation}
\bar{\partial}(g):= \sum\limits_{\alpha\in \mathbb{N}}<e_{\alpha},g> s_{\alpha}, g\in V^*
\end{equation}

where $\{s_k, s_k^*\}_{k=1}^{\infty}$ are generators of the Cuntz algebra $O_{\infty}$.
